      "The Neris flows through the uplands of eastern Lithuania, where it has cut deeply: below the mouth of the Vokė it crosses the Baltic Uplands north-westwards, squeezed into a steep-sided valley only 0.5 to 1 km wide and 60 to 70 m deep; after leaving the uplands, its valley widens to 2 to 3 km. As the river cut down it left terrace after terrace, up to nine levels in the eastern valleys.",
